<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Notitia Dignitatum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 400</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Notitia Dignitatum is a late Roman document listing the civil and military offices of the eastern and western empires, compiled around 400 and updated in the west into the 420s. It records the units and commanders of each region, including the Count of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> Shore and his forts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, and survives in illustrated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> copies. It is a major source for the late Roman army and administration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/notitia-dignitatum.jpg" alt="Notitia Dignitatum" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bodl_Canon.Misc.378_roll159B_frame28.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
